CREATED:20260501T161152Z
DESCRIPTION:Running time: 90 minutes\nTickets: FREE! First-come\, first-se
 rved\nFormal talkback session following the film\n\nJoin us in celebratin
 g the 30th Anniversary of ADF's Screen Dance Festival with a documentary\
 , Can You Bring It: Bill T. Jones and D-Man in the Waters. \n\nThe film w
 ill be followed by a Q&A with director\, ADF alum\, and former member of 
 the Bill T. Jones/Arnie Zane Company\, Rosalynde LeBlanc\, Bill T. Jones\
 , and two NC educators and former members of the company\, Andrea E. Wood
 s Valdés\, Chair of Duke Dance Program\, and Janet Lilly\, Professor of D
 ance at the University of North Carolina\, Greensboro.\n\nCan You Bring I
 t: Bill T. Jones and D-Man in the Waters brings to life the creative proc
 ess that culminated in choreographer-dancer-director Bill T. Jones's tour
  de force ballet D-Man in the Waters\, one of the most important works of
  art to come out of the AIDS crisis. In 1989\, D-Man in the Waters gave p
 hysical manifestation to the fear\, anger\, grief\, and hope for salvatio
 n that the emerging Bill T. Jones/Arnie Zane Company felt as they were em
 battled by the AIDS epidemic. As a group of young dancers in the present 
 re-interpret the work\, they deepen their understanding of its power-expl
 oring what is at stake in their own personal lives in order to commit and
  perform it successfully. Through an extraordinary collage of interviews\
 , archival material\, and uniquely powerful cinematography\, this lyrical
  documentary uses the story of this iconic dance to illustrate the power 
 of art and the triumph of the human spirit. Winner of a 2024 Peabody Awar
 d!
DURATION:PT1H30M
DTSTAMP:20260501T161152Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260621T190000
LAST-MODIFIED:20260501T161152Z
